To: tru64-unix-managers
Subject: Summary: Fortran style printing
X-MARC-Message: https://marc.info/?l=tru64-unix-managers&m=96079343919674

Several people were kind enough to point out that remote printers cannot
benefit from the "-f" option on lpr. The widely recommended way around
this is to pipe the output file via a filter. For us, the best option to
use is the fpr filter, which was suggested by Richard Jackson. I have
tested fpr with lpr and mpage and both now work fine when printing files
that contain FORTRAN carriage control.

