>From Steve Hancock <shancock@zk3.dec.com>:

Hi Jerome,

Thanks for asking about my forthcoming book ...

The book is currently in the final stages of publication. The
latest information I have from Digital Press is the book should 
be on the shelves by mid-summer. The delay in publishing was due 
primarily to my lateness in getting the manuscript to the publisher 
by the original deadline. I felt the book was not ready at that 
time, so DP gave me some extra time with it. I apologize for that, 
but I think the result will be worth the wait.

As far as what I cover ... it is designed to be comprehensive; 
including everything from the basics (creating file systems) to 
quite advanced (tuning and troubleshooting). I think the text will 
be useful as a reference guide and for those looking to learn how to 
really get the most out of their Tru64 UNIX file systems. I have 
included lots (hundreds) of practical examples to make understanding 
the concepts as easy as possible. 

The book was geared to TruCluster 5.x, but I try to point out where things 
are applicable to prior versions. I focus on AdvFS, but I have an
entire chapter devoted to UFS. The Table of Contents will be the 
following:

Ch. 1   Introduction
Ch. 2   Storage and Device Management
Ch. 3   Logical Storage Manager
Ch. 4   File Systems Architecture (VFS)
Ch. 5   UNIX File System
Ch. 6   Intro to AdvFS
Ch. 7   Advanced Topics in AdvFS
Ch. 8   Configuration and Tuning
Ch. 9   Troubleshooting and Recovery

App A   Freeware Tools
