Subject: SUMMARY Tru64 5.0 on DEC 3000
X-MARC-Message: https://marc.info/?l=tru64-unix-managers&m=96079343919630

Hallo!

> Did anybody ever try to run Tru64 UNIX version 5.0 on a DEC 3000 station,
> and is this a supported configuration?

I have received lots of mails from users that successfully run this
configuration. So I don't expect any problems.

A very valuable clarification as to the degree of supportedness of this
configuration I received from Dr. Tom Blinn (tpb@doctor.zk3.dec.com). He
stated that

  - The DEC 3000 series IS supported by Tru64 5.0 and WILL BE supported 
    by later versions of the operating system.
  - Support for add-on turbochannel graphics options has been or will
    be removed in 5.0 or later versions. On-board graphics adapters,
    however, will continue to be supported.
  - The latest "unattended install" feature will not work on DEC 3000
    models. This is not to be confused with RIS - RIS will work.

Thanks to all who replied to my question.

Kind Regards,
Tobias Ernst [Physik CIP Pool, University of Stuttgart]

