this might help you out.

Tony

1.1 TruCluster Tuning Details
=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=
=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D
Due to the site separation of the two cluster member, certain cluster
specific network timers have been tuned to account for potential =
latency in
network response. The current values can be obtained via the asemgr =
utility
('a', 'C').
In order to override the defaults set in the ASE database the file
/etc/hsm.conf has been created and populated with the following values =
in
tenths of seconds:
HSM_PNET_MR=3D8           # Primary network maximum retries
HSM_ANET_MR=3D8           # Backup network maximum retries

This was not applicable as it was not multi site, fibre and I don't =
think it
was to do with network timings and retries, as with just the heatbeat =
and
main network all worked fine. It seemed a more fundamental problem with =
the
additional interfaces interfering somehow.
