From: Massimo Gais <mgais () na ! astro ! it>
Date: Thu, 13 Apr 2000 10:17:46 +0000
To: tru64-unix-managers
Subject: SUMMARY: How to change CDE login
X-MARC-Message: https://marc.info/?l=tru64-unix-managers&m=96079343919451


After hint from Peter.Stern@weizmann.ac.il

I began to read dtlogin man page, so at last
I discovered that in /etc/dt/config
the installation of the Italian subset created
a file Xconfig with this:

#include "/usr/dt/config/Xconfig"
Dtlogin*language: it_IT.ISO8859-1

Simply commenting out the Dtlogin*language
reverted the system to its previous behaviour.

Massimo Gais                               <mgais@na.astro.it>
