From: Bill Antoniadis <sysadmin () horseracinginfo ! com>
Date: Wed, 05 Apr 2000 13:11:53 +0000
To: tru64-unix-managers
Subject: SUMMARY: Install 4.0F or 5.0?
X-MARC-Message: https://marc.info/?l=tru64-unix-managers&m=96079343919346

Hello,

First, I want to to sincerely thank everyone (15 or so) who responded to
my question of whether I should install 4.0F (or another version of DU4.0) or 
5.0 on a server running iPlanet's Enterprise Server.

While most people running DU5.0 appreciate some of it's new features, almost 
everyone suggested installing DU4.0F for the following reasons:

1. DU5.0 has some issues that need to be ironed out.
2. DU5.0's shared libraries are different than DU4.0x and some things may
   not run properly.
3. iPlanet's Enterprise Server is not yet certified for DU5.0.
4. iPlanet will not offer support for DU5.0
5. DU4.0F is very stable.
6. Eventually I would need to upgrade to DU4.0F to jump to DU5.0, so any other 
   installation of a version of DU4.0, would be a waste of time.

Many thanks again,
Bill Antoniadis

