Date: Mon, 03 Apr 2000 21:10:52 +0000
To: tru64-unix-managers
Subject: SUMMARY: Networker 5.5 will not see the TL891 jukebox
X-MARC-Message: https://marc.info/?l=tru64-unix-managers&m=96079343919315

I posted the original partial summary for this question in September 1999. I
was having problems with Networker 5.5.1 seeing my TL891 and I have seen
other people post questions about this issue.  I have just received the
resolution from a Legato SE who was on-site.

Resolution :

When running NW 5.5.1 the inquire does not see the TLxxx jukebox.
This has been seen with both the TL891 and TL895.
- It has been confirmed that the O/S is properly identifying the jukebox, 
but the inquire simply does not report it.

In both cases these jukeboxes were being recognized by the firmware to the 
O/S as TL810 or TL800 (respectively)

Impact:
As a result of this the jb_config can not be used in 'autodetect' mode.

Workaround:

Use "#uerf -r 300 -R | more"  to obtain the correct scsi address and
firmware
recognition.
______________
... (excerpt of the output of the above uerf command)
    scsi1 at pza0 slot 0
     changer at scsi1 target 0 lun 0 (LID=1) (DEC     TL810    (C) DEC 2.20)
...
_________________
OR
Use "# scu show edt bus 1"  (assuming that the jukebox is on Bus 1)
________________________
CAM Equipment Device Table (EDT) Information:

     Device: TL810      Bus: 1, Target: 0, Lun: 0, Type: Medium Changer
___________________________

1. Run jb_config and specify Option #3 SJI device
2. Then select the appropriate option for the DLT device
(#41 Digital DLT800 series, #42 Digital DLT810 series, #43 Digital DLT820 
series)and specify scsidev@1.0.0 (depending on the result from the 'scu'
command)

I suspect that the fix for this will be available with NW 5.5.1-001, but 
that is not
confirmed at this time

